# Force LF in the working tree on EVERY platform, overriding a runner's core.autocrlf. Without this, the
# windows-latest CI runner (autocrlf=true by default) checks out our LF-committed files as CRLF, and
# `oxfmt --check` (endOfLine: lf) then flags every file. text=auto lets git still auto-detect binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries — never normalize / never get an EOL applied.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
